        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "Terminal-started recordings stopped by the agent's record hotkey get no dialog (the hotkey acts like `peep stop`); the dialog is for recordings the agent started \u2014 the manifest constraint read literally",
            "Pressing the record hotkey while the naming dialog is open keeps the automatic name (Esc semantics) and starts the next take",
            "Last-used collection means the collection the agent's last dialog outcome left a take in, persisted in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\peep\\agent-prefs.json; terminal recordings do not change it"
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "Startup entry is a .lnk written by PowerShell's WScript.Shell COM object, not a .cmd (a .cmd flashes a console at every login)",
            "Marks: one request file per press (mark-<ns>-<pid>.json) rather than a single `mark` file, so two presses inside one 100 ms poll are two marks; `t` is the press time from the request's wall clock, not the poll time",
            "Delete in the dialog is the discard key in both fields (Backspace still edits); Up/Down cycle collections from either field so they are one keystroke away",
            "The agent's own commands (stop, reload) ride a second control file, agent-command, beside A's stop-request; agent.json is its pidfile/status; a named mutex is the race-free single-instance guard",
            "Hotkeys live on a dedicated Win32 message-loop thread, not Tk's; every piece of agent logic runs on the Tk thread through a non-reentrant dispatcher so A's flash update() loop cannot re-enter it",
            "catalog gains a `discarded` event and the fold drops it (A's fold ignored unknown events, so a discarded take would otherwise stay listed)",
            "The installed-copy staleness check runs only when `wsl --list --running` names the distro, because touching \\\\wsl.localhost would boot WSL at login",
            "Overlays (pill and toasts) are secured with capture exclusion while fully transparent, before anything is drawn"
          ],
